00:07:39,930 --> 00:07:42,390
that's exactly
what I expected.

279
00:07:42,390 --> 00:07:44,130
What was different
was that for the

280
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,450
first time in two
years I'd done

281
00:07:46,450 --> 00:07:48,650
something for my
knee instead of to

282
00:07:48,650 --> 00:07:49,400
it.

283
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,550
Twenty minutes,
in my own chair,

284
00:07:51,550 --> 00:07:52,650
after work.

285
00:07:52,650 --> 00:07:54,580
No drive, no copay.

286
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:56,100
They say
twenty minutes.

287
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,180
I did thirty,

288
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,300
twice a day,

289
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:00,370
lowest setting
that first week.

290
00:08:00,370 --> 00:08:01,900
I put it on the calendar.

291
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:02,740
The first week,

292
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:04,330
I couldn't have told
you if anything

293
00:08:04,330 --> 00:08:05,500
was happening.

294
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,840
I tried not to
get my hopes

295
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:07,520
up.

296
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,890
I'd had things
help for a week

297
00:08:08,890 --> 00:08:10,090
and then stop.

298
00:08:10,090 --> 00:08:11,550
But somewhere in
the second week I

299
00:08:11,550 --> 00:08:13,340
noticed I'd come down
the stairs without

300
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:15,010
holding the rail.

301
00:08:15,010 --> 00:08:16,560
I hadn't decided to.

302
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:17,620
I just did it,

303
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:19,120
then stopped halfway
down because I

304
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,290
realized.

305
00:08:20,290 --> 00:08:22,100
By the end of
the fourth week

306
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,250
I'd slept through
the night four times

307
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:25,270
running.

308
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:26,390
I stood at the counter

309
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:28,230
and finished making
dinner without looking

310
00:08:28,230 --> 00:08:29,730
for the stool.

311
00:08:29,730 --> 00:08:31,510
None of that is dramatic.

312
00:08:31,510 --> 00:08:33,030
All of it was gone for two

313
00:08:33,030 --> 00:08:34,080
years.

314
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:36,170
A few weeks later
my wife asked

315
00:08:36,170 --> 00:08:37,820
if I wanted to
walk the long

316
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:39,450
way around the block.

317
00:08:39,450 --> 00:08:40,820
And for the
first time in two

318
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:42,740
years, I said yes.

319
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:44,520
I wanted to
understand why,

320
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:46,350
so I read the
whole thing.

321
00:08:46,350 --> 00:08:48,230
It comes down
to four steps.

322
00:08:48,230 --> 00:08:49,120
One.

323
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,110
The tissue around
a new knee can

324
00:08:51,110 --> 00:08:54,750
stay inflamed long
after surgery is over.

325
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:55,580
Two.

326
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:58,030
Inflamed tissue
holds extra fluid,

327
00:08:58,030 --> 00:08:59,570
so it takes up
more room than

328
00:08:59,570 --> 00:09:00,460
it should.

329
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:00,830
Three.

330
00:09:00,830 --> 00:09:02,880
There's only so
much room in there.

331
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:04,590
Bending compresses it.

332
00:09:04,590 --> 00:09:06,390
Straightening
pulls it tight.

333
00:09:06,390 --> 00:09:08,020
That's the squeeze.

334
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:09,210
Four.

335
00:09:09,210 --> 00:09:11,860
Red and near-infrared
light have been studied

336
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:13,780
for calming that
inflammation,

337
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:15,230
so the swelling and
the pressure can

338
00:09:15,230 --> 00:09:16,270
come down with it.

339
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:18,080
In a randomized trial,

340
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:20,020
patients given light
therapy after a knee

341
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:21,880
replacement
had less pain,

342
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:24,580
less swelling and better
early movement than

343
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:25,670
those who weren't.

344
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:28,540
A 2025 review
said the same,

345
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:30,160
and was clear the
evidence is still

346
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:31,030
limited.

347
00:09:31,030 --> 00:09:32,730
I probably sound
like a broken record

348
00:09:32,730 --> 00:09:34,000
to my family
and the guys on

349
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,070
my crew.

350
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:37,140
But after two years
of doing everything

351
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:39,040
I was told and
getting nowhere,

352
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:40,500
you have no idea
what it's like

353
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:41,760
to sleep through
the night,

354
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,210
say yes to the walk,

355
00:09:43,210 --> 00:09:44,700
and get my life back.

356
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,690
So take it from me.

357
00:09:46,690 --> 00:09:48,490
Don't spend another
year waiting for it

358
00:09:48,490 --> 00:09:49,270
to settle.

359
00:09:49,270 --> 00:09:51,230
Don't spend two
hundred a session.

360
00:09:51,230 --> 00:09:53,180
More than ten thousand
people with pain

361
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:55,340
after a knee replacement
have already tried

362
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:56,040
this.

363
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,990
Some had it
worse than I did.

364
00:09:57,990 --> 00:09:59,830
You can get the
KenRelief wrap from

365
00:09:59,830 --> 00:10:02,720
their website, with
a discount link

366
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,840
and ninety days to try it.

367
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,850
If it doesn't do
anything for you,

368
00:10:06,850 --> 00:10:08,260
